# Nexly — Core Rules

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript strict, Prisma + PostgreSQL, Better Auth, Tailwind + shadcn/ui
- pnpm only — never npm or yarn
- No `any` in TypeScript

## Design System
- Dark-themed UI, minimalist aesthetic
- Purple/lavender accents for primary actions and highlights
- Mobile-first responsive design on all new components

## Architecture
- API logic in `/app/api` or server actions only — never in client components
- Server components by default; `"use client"` only when interactivity requires it
- Always read `prisma/schema.prisma` before suggesting UI changes that touch data
- Run `prisma migrate dev` after schema changes; never skip migrations

## Collaboration Features
- Bidirectional approval logic for brand ↔ creator collaboration flows
- Both parties must confirm before a collaboration is marked active

## Code Style
- One responsibility per component/file
- No inline styles — Tailwind only
- No comments narrating what code does; only explain non-obvious intent
- Optimistic UI updates where beneficial; avoid unnecessary full-page reloads
